WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.460
While it isn't stated outright, "Black Panther:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:06.000
Wakanda Forever" heavily implies that&nbsp;
M'Baku gained a high-ranking position&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.240
in the African nation. The actor&nbsp;
who plays him all but confirmed it.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.780
Wakanda undergoes a lot of changes&nbsp;
during "Black Panther: Wakanda Forever."

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.300
"This movie is so much."

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.780
The film begins with the death of&nbsp;
King T'Challa, who was played by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.980
the late Chadwick Boseman. M'Baku becomes&nbsp;
an advisor to the Wakandan royal family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:27.720
helping Shuri as she grieves. T'Challa and&nbsp;
Shuri's mother, Queen Ramonda, takes the throne.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.720
After a fight in Boston that&nbsp;
leads to Shuri being kidnapped,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:35.640
Ramonda takes away Okoye's title as General&nbsp;
of the Dora Milaje, claiming that Okoye is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:40.320
failing in her role as protector. Queen Ramonda&nbsp;
is then killed when Talokan attacks Wakanda with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:44.340
a flood. As Shuri struggles with the sudden&nbsp;
deaths of her brother and mother, she decides&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.120
to step into the suit of the Black Panther,&nbsp;
becoming the ultimate protector of Wakanda.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:52.320
It's a lot to pack into two hours and 41&nbsp;
minutes, but the movie still has room for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:56.400
more storylines. As the film continues to&nbsp;
add depth to the characters established&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.120
in 2018's "Black Panther," several&nbsp;
new characters also into the fold.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:05.700
That includes MIT student — and future Ironheart&nbsp;
— Riri Williams and Namor, who rules over Talokan.

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:09.240
By the end of the movie, it seems that&nbsp;
Shuri is now the official leader of Wakanda,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:12.000
but Winston Duke, who plays&nbsp;
M'Baku, begs to differ.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:18.243
New cutaway, M’baku chanting.&nbsp;
End after mask is removed

00:01:18.243 --> 00:01:18.900
Shuri&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:22.980
may be the new Black Panther, but Duke&nbsp;
has confirmed that M'Baku is, in fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.560
the new king of Wakanda. He recently told Esquire,

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:29.220
"Yeah, it's kind of cool, though, being revealed&nbsp;
as the king of Wakanda at the end of the movie."

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:33.780
M'Baku was first introduced in "Black Panther"&nbsp;
as the leader of the Jabari Tribe. He challenges&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:37.980
T'Challa for the throne of Wakanda following&nbsp;
the death of T'Challa's father T'Chaka.

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:46.080
"I, M'Baku, leader of the Jabari--"&nbsp;
"I accept your challenge."

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:49.680
T'Challa, who had already taken on the&nbsp;
role of Black Panther years earlier,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:52.200
defeats M'Baku, replacing his father as king.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.720
There is a callback to this duel&nbsp;
at the end of "Black Panther:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:58.620
Wakanda Forever." The ceremony to&nbsp;
make Shuri queen of Wakanda has begun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:03.360
but Shuri isn't here: she has decided to visit&nbsp;
Nakia in Haiti, where Shuri meets her nephew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:06.780
Nakia and T'Challa's son. When Shuri&nbsp;
doesn't arrive at Warrior Falls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:11.220
the title of king instead appears to be up for&nbsp;
M'Baku to claim, with no visible challengers.

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:15.420
Shuri's absence at the ceremony could be&nbsp;
interpreted as a forfeit, making M'Baku&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:19.020
the new king of Wakanda. Regardless,&nbsp;
Duke called the moment huge, saying,

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:21.180
"Whatever that entails,&nbsp;
that's gonna be a fun one."

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:24.660
So what does it take to be king of&nbsp;
Wakanda? According to Winston Duke,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.420
it's all about putting the&nbsp;
people first. He told Esquire,

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:31.500
"I think any power of authority and leadership&nbsp;
is gonna be defined by their willingness to think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.860
of the greater good for everyone, instead&nbsp;
of their own personal needs and agendas."

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:38.100
Duke noted that there are still plenty&nbsp;
more stories to tell in this part of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:42.180
the MCU. Of course, that could include his&nbsp;
potential reign in Wakanda. While Duke said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:45.120
he would love to see at least four&nbsp;
more movies in the Black Panther saga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:49.560
he also brought up the idea of a possible spin-off&nbsp;
for his character and the Jabari Tribe. He said,

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:52.680
"They are an entity unto themselves in&nbsp;
the mountains. [...] And I feel like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.680
if you got a spin-off, that we get&nbsp;
to learn what things mean, and why,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:59.460
and why they're special, and dive into that&nbsp;
culture, it would be something really special."

